"shares":3101.0,"price_per_share":151.8064,"dollar_value":470751.65,"shares_after":80370.0},{"date":"2026-11-02","insider_name":"TREFF DOUGLAS J","title":"","is_officer":false,"is_director":true,"transaction_code":"S","transaction_type":"sell","shares":7185.0,"price_per_share":152.8515,"dollar_value":1098238.03,"shares_after":73185.0},{"date":"2026-11-02","insider_name":"TREFF DOUGLAS J","title":"","is_officer":false,"is_director":true,"transaction_code":"S","transaction_type":"sell","shares":1100.0,"price_per_share":153.7014,"dollar_value":169071.54,"shares_after":72085.0},{"date":"2026-10-30","insider_name":"Campbell Rupert George","title":"EVP, Brand President, HEYDUDE","is_officer":true,"is_director":false,"transaction_code":"S","transaction_type":"sell","shares":2645.0,"price_per_share":150.8713,"dollar_value":399054.59,"shares_after":68573.0},{"date":"2026-10-30","insider_name":"FRASCH RONALD","title":"","is_officer":false,"is_director":true,"transaction_code":"S","transaction_type":"sell","shares":15000.0,"price_per_share":153.5106,"dollar_value":2302659.0,"shares_after":61180.0}],"_trap_components":{"decline":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.25},"balance_sheet":{"score":0.484,"weight":0.2},"value_destruction":{"score":0.75,"weight":0.2},"derating":{"score":0.018,"weight":0.15},"market":{"score":0.115,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 4% operating margin is roughly in line with the Consumer Cyclical median (8%).","It captures well under its share of sector profits (0.45x its revenue share).","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-19.7% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 377 companies in the universe; the top four hold 26% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 53% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the top of its 52-week range, 6% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 51% and a beta of 1.13, it moves roughly with the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $124.1M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 75% in the 2020 crash, 65% in the 2022 bear market and 98% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 41% below its DCF fair value of $259, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 16%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $162 to $414 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 11.5 vs 19.3, EV/EBITDA 8.4 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 10.5 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 250% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 9.5% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 1.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 12 covering analysts target $165 on average, 8% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 34% clears the cost of capital of 9.6% by 25pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.28).","It runs a 52% gross margin and converts 16% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is a concern: high accruals (-19.0% of assets).","It spends 0.7% of revenue on R&D and 0.9% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.8x net debt to EBITDA ($130.4M of cash against $1.2B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.7x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.8, in the safe zone).","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 1.5 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.4% over 3 years, 23.9% over 5 years and 14.0% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 21%).","At current returns, reinvesting 34% of profits supports about 11.7% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 24.0% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 39, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 10.8% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 3.2%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 4 purchases and 19 sales over the past year, net $20.2M sold.","It returns 8.4% a year to shareholders (8.4% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 4.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 13.4% of the float, 3.8 days to cover."],"people":["With about 8,010 employees, each generates about $504K of revenue, 1.3x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 10.5% a year.","That works out to $82K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.5M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":80,"head":"Invest: trades 41% below fair value of $259; ROIC 34.2% vs WACC 9.6%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 52, gates 12/25)","Trades 41% below fair value of $259","ROIC 34.2% vs WACC 9.6%","FCF margin 16.3%","Revenue grew 23.9%/yr over 5y"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 4.8x","Interest coverage only 1.7x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":219.81,"vc":{"base":258.6,"base_src":"dcf","bear":162.11,"bull":414.13,"alt_median":186.36,"n_alt":1,"gap":0.3877,"dispersion":0.1624,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"CROX","date":"2026-11-06"}